# Firebase web config. Copy this file to `.env` and paste your project's values.
#
# Where to get them:
#   1. https://console.firebase.google.com → Add project (free Spark plan)
#   2. Build → Authentication → Get started → enable "Email/Password"
#   3. Project settings → General → Your apps → Add app → Web (</>)
#   4. Copy the `firebaseConfig` values into the blanks below
#
# These are NOT secrets. Firebase web config is public by design — every client
# app ships it, and it is visible in any decompiled binary. What actually
# protects your data is Firestore security rules plus Firebase Auth. Never put
# a service-account key or admin credential in this file.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ is required: Expo only inlines variables with that prefix into
# the client bundle. Renaming them will silently yield `undefined` at runtime.

EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
